    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for net-tools",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for net-tools fixes the following issues:\n\n- Fix stack buffer overflow in parse_hex (bsc#1248687, GHSA-h667-qrp8-gj58).\n- Fix stack-based buffer overflow in proc_gen_fmt (bsc#1248687, GHSA-w7jq-cmw2-cq59).\n- Avoid unsafe memcpy in ifconfig (bsc#1248687).\n- Prevent overflow in ax25 and netrom (bsc#1248687)\n- Keep possibility to enter long interface names, even if they are\n  not accepted by the kernel, because it was always possible up to\n  CVE-2025-46836 fix. But issue a warning about an interface name\n  concatenation (bsc#1248410).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SLES-16.0-454",
        "title": "Patchnames"
